        {
          "title": "Agent Drift: Quantifying Behavioral Degradation in Multi-Agent LLM Systems Over Extended Interactions",
          "title_zh": "智能体漂移：量化多智能体 LLM 系统在长期交互中的行为退化",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.04170v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2601.04170",
          "summary": "The paper defines agent drift as progressive degradation of agent behavior, decision quality and inter-agent coherence over extended interaction sequences, distinguishing semantic, coordination and behavioral drift. It proposes the Agent Stability Index across twelve dimensions, and theoretical analysis suggests that episodic memory consolidation, drift-aware routing protocols and adaptive behavioral anchoring can reduce drift-related errors.",
